<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020, 2023) & Matsuda et al. (2020) human pluripotent stem-cell segmentation clock and metabolic tempo scaling model — MorphoEval overall 91.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py` (91.7/100, up from 60.3/100 in Pass 1; +31.4 overall). The remediated script solves the delayed autoinhibitory HES7 mRNA/protein DDE with parabolic peak refinement, reproducing the 2.4591x tempo slowdown from mouse WT (122.00 min) to human WT iPSC-PSM (300.01 min = 5.0 h), verifying exact tempo rescaling collapse across lambda in [1.0, 3.0] (max std = 2.32e-13 nM, linear r = 1.0000), evaluating all 6 Matsuda (2020) & Diaz-Cuadros (2020, 2023) genetic and mitochondrial NAD+/NADH regimes (Pearson r = 0.9999, RMSE = 2.18 min, including intronless Hes7 subcritical Hopf collapse to T = 0 min), modeling 6-species vertebrate clock allometry across a 10-fold period range (30 min to 300 min, r = 0.9970), rendering a human axioloid traveling-wave kymograph, and segmenting bilateral paraxial somite rows on `human_somite_organoid_specimen.jpg` (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010), backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_028_human_somite_organoid_clock.lean`. Overall 91.5/100 (faithfulness 91.4, reproducibility 91.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 93, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/human_somite_organoid_clock_comparison.png: rendered output of 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 1497613 B, 2775×1650 px, artifact_sha256 6905f3a436b14604460fee8b7dc21933782bad0682b62a8fcef0ec1177557d7f (sha256 6905f3a436b14604460fee8b7dc21933782bad0682b62a8fcef0ec1177557d7f), spec_fingerprint 660586c9076da1ed7c1ed1d6e1b6ce7158ddbb20e73624b4efa3112652481b95. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 660586c9076da1ed7c1ed1d6e1b6ce7158ddbb20e73624b4efa3112652481b95; artifact_sha256: 6905f3a436b14604460fee8b7dc21933782bad0682b62a8fcef0ec1177557d7f; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/human_somite_organoid_clock_reference.json=0215c114f029234a..., datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/human_somite_organoid_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/scout_manifest.json=a3af01b1b2956954...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-human-somite-organoid-clock-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020) Nature 580:113-118 discovery of ~5.0 h (300 min) HES7-Achilles oscillations in human pluripotent stem-cell-derived presomitic mesoderm vs ~2.0 h (122 min) in mouse PSM | Matsuda et al. (2020) Science 369:1450-1455 demonstration that species-specific HES7 intron splicing delay (tau_tx) and protein/mRNA half-lives (t_1/2), rather than the hHES7 genomic locus sequence alone, govern the 2.5x human clock slowdown | Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2023) Nature 613:550-557 demonstration that mitochondrial electron transport chain activity and cytosolic NAD+/NADH ratio modulate global translation rate and segmentation clock period (LbNOX acceleration vs sodium azide/rotenone slowdown); reconstructed_in_script: Delayed autoinhibitory HES7 transcriptional-translational feedback loop (TTFL) RK2 DDE solver reproducing mouse WT (122.00 min), human WT (300.01 min, ratio = 2.4591), and exact tempo rescaling collapse (std = 2.32e-13 nM, linear r = 1.0000) | 6-regime genetic & metabolic perturbation series (mouse WT, mouse + hHES7 swap, human WT, human + LbNOX NAD+ rescue, human + sodium azide ETC inhibition, and intronless Hes7 subcritical collapse; Pearson r = 0.9999, RMSE = 2.18 min) | 6-species vertebrate segmentation clock allometry (r = 0.9970), human axioloid traveling-wave kymograph, and bilateral dorsal somite row DoG segmentation on human_somite_organoid_specimen.jpg (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010); transfer_boundary: Single-cell and 1D/2D axioloid HES7 DDE kinetics compared with dorsal vertebrate paraxial somite SEM metameric periodicity; does_not_claim: Full 3D actomyosin apical constriction mechanics during epithelial somite rosette clefting." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the single-cell delayed HES7 TTFL oscillator to intercellular DLL1-Notch delay coupling across a 2D hexagonal presomitic mesoderm lattice to model phase-synchronization recovery after DAPT washout.",
        "remediation needed: Incorporate explicit Matrigel-embedded mechanical boundary forces during human axioloid epithelial somite rosette formation (Yamanaka et al. 2023)." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.15e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

